@@ -3,3 +3,16 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns the value of `document` that
+`pointer` refers to. The empty pointer returns the whole document.
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (it must be empty or start with `/`,
+and `~` may only be followed by `0` or `1`), or when it does not resolve to a value of the document: a
+missing member, an array index that is out of range, has a leading zero or is `-`, or a step into a
+scalar or `null`. Only own members of objects are followed, so `__proto__` and similar names never reach
+the prototype chain.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
